// CotSC: English translation extracted from bg0700_baldurs_gate.d
// Original English strings preserved exactly. Translate text inside ~...~ only.

@1 = ~Flaming Fist is absolutely awful. Each time the officer that patrols the streets by my workplace, she always sends me that disgusted look. They think they are above the law because they enforce it. Pathetic.~
@2 = ~Chill... that group of Bandit hogboblins... they once tried to recruit me. Once I refused they beat me up bad and threatened that if they see me again, I won't be so lucky. Dear Selune, I even experienced hate crime firsthand here in Baldur's Gate for being the same race. How is that fair? Majority of said bandits were human, and we do not spread prejudice over that, do we?~
@3 = ~Me don't sight you well.~
@4 = ~What?~
@5 = ~Me not sight... no. Me not love... you?~
@6 = ~You don't like me, you mean?~
@7 = ~Yes... yes. Me bad language. Me learn. Me sorry.~
@8 = ~My father says heroism is determined by the deeds, not looks. My intention isn't to sound rude but... you don't give me good vibes. Don't get mad over it. I am simply voicing my opinion out loud.~
@9 = ~All my friends find it hard to determine which of these taverns offer better ale. Elfsong or Purple Wyrm Inn. What do you think?~
@10 = ~I can't believe how problematic it is to get a job in this city. Well prospering city on lips of the entire Sword Coast but when it comes to employability the chances dwindle each day.~
@11 = ~Another magic wielding, trouble-making riffraff. Just stay away from our children. Last thing we need is them following your footsteps and getting themselves killed over a notion of chasing fame and wealth. Find an honest work instead, you fopdoodles.~
@12 = ~The prices for fabric from the North is absolutely ourtageous. How am I suppose to afford it. It's beautiful and made out of  shimmerweave. Luxurious, classy and undeniably pretty.~
@13 = ~I hope you aren't here to slaughter me like a pig. All I want is enjoy the fair. Some armored passersby sometimes look at me like I am a monster.~
@14 = ~Have a nice day.~
@15 = ~Out of the way, please! I am on my way to the Duke's Palace. They need to be informed about potential resource gathering of the Amnian forces. Dark times are indeed upon us.~
@16 = ~My mom said not to talk to strangers.~
@17 = ~Weather is horrible in this city. Constant rain. I blame Umberlee and her damned temple in this city.~
@18 = ~Listen to my advice, stranger. Never get married. Ever! My husband is seeing another woman for over a year. And I doubt she is the only one. He is good looking, he knows that. I just wish we could rekindle an old flame. I allow it to happen because he is a breadwinner and I don't have a job. Maybe that's why he grew distant. He finds me useless.~
@19 = ~I... believe you're right. The feeling clearly isn't mutual. I'll leave Damian. He can do as he pleases with that other woman. From now on, I am free as a bird and willing to take my life into my owns hands.~
@20 = ~As someone who is currently married I can give you an advice. He isn't worth your time. Love is a mutual feeling that glues two people together in a shared feelings of respect, loyalty and passion. If one spouse strays off that path, it will lead to marriage's downfall. Woman to a woman. Leave him and find someone loving you for who you are.~
@21 = ~This fair is nothing compared to Nashkel's infamous Carnival. I should visit one day. Now, that the city is open again I can make a trip.~
